x11 bridge: stop advertising MIT-SHM to the guest

The bridge forwards a QueryExtension for MIT-SHM to the host server and passes
the reply back untouched, so a guest client concludes the extension is usable.
It is not. The bridge proxies DRI3, SYNC and Present; nothing translates a
shared-memory segment, so the client goes on to name a SysV id that means
nothing in the host's IPC namespace, and the connection dies on ShmAttach.

Rewriting the name it asks after leaves the server answering for an extension
nobody implements, and the client takes the fallback path it already carries
for servers without MIT-SHM. The request framing is untouched: the name keeps
its length, only its first byte changes.

Upstream: AsahiLinux/muvm#172, "Major opcode of failed request: 130 (MIT-SHM)",
open since 2025-04-29 with no maintainer reply.

--- a/crates/muvm/src/guest/bridge/x11.rs
+++ b/crates/muvm/src/guest/bridge/x11.rs
@@ -315,6 +315,11 @@
                 return Ok(StreamSendResult::WantMore);
             }
 
+            // This bridge forwards MIT-SHM but does not proxy it, so a guest told the
+            // extension is present sends a SysV id that means nothing to the host.
+            if &buf[8..end] == b"MIT-SHM" {
+                buf[8] = b'X';
+            }
             let name = String::from_utf8_lossy(&buf[8..end]);
             if name == "DRI3" {
                 this.protocol_handler.dri3_qe_resp_seq = Some(this.protocol_handler.seq_no);
